<p style="text-align: left;">The table gives the results of a survey of <math alttext="200"><mn>200</mn>
</math> people who were asked how often they see a movie in a theater. How many people responded either “never” or “almost never”?</p>$SATQ$, $SATQ$[{"id":"2a0d8ff9-70a5-46ca-9dc5-e4f7337351eb","content":"<p><math alttext=\"24\"><mn>24</mn>\n</math></p>"},{"id":"3b4cb061-6024-434f-916d-0e94af153fd9","content":"<p><math alttext=\"53\"><mn>53</mn>\n</math></p>"},{"id":"be36f27c-bbbd-4407-b3d2-63d24f47c7a2","content":"<p><math alttext=\"82\"><mn>82</mn>\n</math></p>"},{"id":"2e331de9-d896-406a-acde-224d540dbfbb","content":"<p><math alttext=\"118\"><mn>118</mn>\n</math></p>"}]$SATQ$::jsonb, $SATQ$["C"]$SATQ$::jsonb, $SATQ$["be36f27c-bbbd-4407-b3d2-63d24f47c7a2"]$SATQ$::jsonb, $SATQ$<p style="text-align: left;">Choice C is correct. The table gives the results of <math alttext="200"><mn>200</mn>
</math> people who were asked how often they see a movie in a theater. The table shows that <math alttext="29"><mn>29</mn>
</math> people responded &ldquo;never&rdquo; and <math alttext="53"><mn>53</mn>
</math> people responded &ldquo;almost never.&rdquo; Therefore, <math alttext="29 plus 53"><mn>29</mn><mo>+</mo><mn>53</mn></math>, or <math alttext="82"><mn>82</mn>
</math>, people responded either &ldquo;never&rdquo; or &ldquo;almost never.&rdquo;</p>
<p style="text-align: left;">Choice A is incorrect. This is the difference between the number of people who responded &ldquo;almost never&rdquo; and the number of people who responded &ldquo;never.&rdquo;</p>
<p style="text-align: left;">Choice B is incorrect. This is the number of people who responded &ldquo;almost never&rdquo; but doesn't include those who responded &ldquo;never.&rdquo;</p>
