<p style="text-align: left;">The box plots summarize the masses, in kilograms, of two groups of gazelles. Based on the box plots, which of the following statements must be true?</p>$SATQ$, $SATQ$[{"id":"7e87474d-bf2a-4f28-a67b-aa33f67991f8","content":"<p style=\"text-align: left;\">The mean mass of group 1 is greater than the mean mass of group 2.</p>"},{"id":"ad5ccedf-eb53-4cf6-96b8-75eb15808250","content":"<p style=\"text-align: left;\">The mean mass of group 1 is less than the mean mass of group 2.</p>"},{"id":"1e2fd939-1c18-4fc7-9195-ac86130bf8f1","content":"<p style=\"text-align: left;\">The median mass of group 1 is greater than the median mass of group 2.</p>"},{"id":"2f9bb7c4-5b85-4dd6-8da3-5e2fdc9d3a6d","content":"<p style=\"text-align: left;\">The median mass of group 1 is less than the median mass of group 2.</p>"}]$SATQ$::jsonb, $SATQ$["C"]$SATQ$::jsonb, $SATQ$["1e2fd939-1c18-4fc7-9195-ac86130bf8f1"]$SATQ$::jsonb, $SATQ$<p style="text-align: left;">Choice C is correct. The median of a data set represented in a box plot is represented by the vertical line within the box. It follows that the median mass of the gazelles in group <math alttext="1"><mn>1</mn>
</math> is <math alttext="25"><mn>25</mn>
</math> kilograms, and the median mass of the gazelles in group <math alttext="2"><mn>2</mn>
</math> is <math alttext="24"><mn>24</mn>
</math> kilograms. Since <math alttext="25"><mn>25</mn>
</math> kilograms is greater than <math alttext="24"><mn>24</mn>
</math> kilograms, the median mass of group <math alttext="1"><mn>1</mn>
</math> is greater than the median mass of group <math alttext="2"><mn>2</mn>
</math>.</p>
<p style="text-align: left;">Choice A is incorrect. The mean mass of each of the two groups cannot be determined from the box plots.</p>
<p style="text-align: left;">Choice B is incorrect. The mean mass of each of the two groups cannot be determined from the box plots.</p>
