rams, of two groups of gazelles. Based on the box plots, which of the following statements must be true?</p>","externalid":"16b20598-30a0-44b7-8771-8c87e56ec14b","templateid":"0a8cd682-0440-44d6-9c04-07cefb288c4a","vaultid":"c11822dd-c249-460f-a8a0-f1ae7c01e0cc","type":"mcq","answerOptions":[{"id":"7e87474d-bf2a-4f28-a67b-aa33f67991f8","content":"<p style=\"text-align: left;\">The mean mass of group 1 is greater than the mean mass of group 2.</p>"},{"id":"ad5ccedf-eb53-4cf6-96b8-75eb15808250","content":"<p style=\"text-align: left;\">The mean mass of group 1 is less than the mean mass of group 2.</p>"},{"id":"1e2fd939-1c18-4fc7-9195-ac86130bf8f1","content":"<p style=\"text-align: left;\">The median mass of group 1 is greater than the median mass of group 2.</p>"},{"id":"2f9bb7c4-5b85-4dd6-8da3-5e2fdc9d3a6d","content":"<p style=\"text-align: left;\">The median mass of group 1 is less than the median mass of group 2.</p>"}],"correct_answer":["C"]},"createDate":1691007959833,"updateDate":1691007959833}$SATQ$::jsonb, 1691007959833, 1691007959833),
    ($SATQ$d4413871$SATQ$, NULL, NULL, $SATQ$019746-DC$SATQ$, $SATQ$disclosed$SATQ$, $SATQ$SAT$SATQ$, 2, $SATQ$Math$SATQ$, $SATQ$Problem-Solving and Data Analysis$SATQ$, $SATQ$Q$SATQ$, $SATQ$Q.E.$SATQ$, $SATQ$Probability and conditional probability$SATQ$, $SATQ$H$SATQ$, 6, $SATQ$spr$SATQ$, $SATQ$<div class="stimulus_reference " xmlns="http://www.imsglobal.org/xsd/apip/apipv1p0/qtiitem/imsqti_v2p1"><div class="passage "><div class="prose style:1 "><p class="passage_para ">&nbsp;</p><div class="table_wrapper "><div class="tcp-e4589060-6a49-4fb9-a72a-23a578e0b2a9"><table class="table_WithBorder tcp-06196331-3edc-4c8f-876b-d57b3d755f43"><tbody><tr><td class="tcp-06743663-cf51-4d3a-bb0f-8b9210f1b926">&nbsp;</td><td class="tcp-9fb58c64-27a2-4be8-8131-1424067761ce" colspan="4" rowspan="1">Blood type&nbsp; &nbsp;</td></tr><tr><td class="tcp-02abeec4-f408-454a-87df-05c7c6994beb">Rhesus factor</td><td class="tcp-f8b24cc8-81fe-48a7-a682-337ede35519b">A</td><td class="tcp-4bf04f05-b26e-49c9-9e89-3fccdbe67aa5">B</td><td class="tcp-028d81ca-d098-4c84-9e84-3620dbeae02c">AB</td><td class="tcp-02b79468-351b-40a0-b9a7-9b2bb86fe635">O</td></tr><tr><td class="tcp-1aac0023-14d4-4475-935e-069fdbf84bcd"><span class="math_expression "><span class="math-container"><img align="middle" role="math" class="math-img" src="https://bkmyfcolrdumyrwktjrr.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/sat-images/d4413871/img_000_63c9f63f.png" alt="plus"></span></span></td><td class="tcp-05f1a050-4c0d-4e64-b64e-c58780bafe88">33</td><td class="tcp-1d324382-0266-4e24-b80c-3fbd65ce08f7">9</td><td class="tcp-a7adcf0c-ce15-4409-a2e0-667ee9a895e3">3</td><td class="tcp-37dd5d78-47ee-41d7-8c67-420e63f5e677">37</td></tr><tr><td class="tcp-5a3393db-bbc3-4009-b4fc-634ae86ebf04"><span class="math_expression "><span class="math-container"><img align="middle" role="math" class="math-img" src="https://bkmyfcolrdumyrwktjrr.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/sat-images/d4413871/img_001_79bab492.png" alt="minus"></span></span></td><td class="tcp-bd3f95aa-f701-461c-a4d3-ab4c2b64b2ac">7</td><td class="tcp-3ac2333f-1894-4587-9a4e-16bf77125399">2</td><td class="tcp-54b95007-a3cd-44d2-a670-cbf65d2b6c54">1</td><td class="tcp-c50c8657-2486-4a4d-bcfa-e1718c1aee53"><span class="italic"><span class="italic ">x</span></span></td></tr></tbody></table></div></div></div></div></div>
$SATQ$, $SATQ$<p class="stem_paragraph ">Human blood can be classified into four common blood types&mdash;A, B, AB, and O. It is also characterized by the presence <span class="math-container"><img align="middle" role="math" class="math-img" src="https://bkmyfcolrdumyrwktjrr.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/sat-images/d4413871/img_002_e040f3b4.png" alt="open parenthesis, plus, close parenthesis"></span> or absence <span class="math-container"><img align="middle" role="math" class="math-img" src="https://bkmyfcolrdumyrwktjrr.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/sat-images/d4413871/img_003_46d9fd76.png" alt="open parenthesis, minus, close parenthesis"></span> of the rhesus factor. The table above shows the distribution of blood type and rhesus factor for a group of people. If one of these people who is rhesus negative <span class="math-container"><img align="middle" role="math" class="math-img" src="https://bkmyfcolrdumyrwktjrr.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/sat-images/d4413871/img_004_46d9fd76.png" alt="open parenthesis, minus, close parenthesis"></span> is chosen at random, the probability that the person has blood type B is <span class="math_expression "><span class="math-container"><img align="middle" role="math" class="math-img" src="https://bkmyfcolrdumyrwktjrr.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/sat-images/d4413871/img_005_e367f6c9.png" alt="one ninth"></span></span> . What is the value of <span class="italic">x</span> ?</p>
$SATQ$, NULL, $SATQ$["8"]$SATQ$::jsonb, NULL, $SATQ$<p>The correct answer is 8. In this group, <span class="math-container"><img align="middle" role="math" class="math-img" src="https://bkmyfcolrdumyrwktjrr.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/sat-images/d4413871/img_006_e367f6c9.png" alt="one ninth"></span> of the people who are rhesus negative have blood type B. The total number of people who are rhesus negative in the group is <span class="math-container"><img align="middle" role="math" class="math-img" src="https://bkmyfcolrdumyrwktjrr.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/sat-images/d4413871/img_007_26860f98.png" alt="7 plus 2, plus 1, plus x"></span>, and there are 2 people who are rhesus negative with blood type B. Therefore, <span class="math-container"><img align="middle" role="math" class="math-img" src="https://bkmyfcolrdumyrwktjrr.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/sat-images/d4413871/img_008_0d0e084f.png" alt="the fraction with numerator 2, and denominator, 7 plus 2, plus 1, plus x, end fraction, equals one ninth"></span>. Combining like terms on the left-hand side of the equation yields <span class="math-container"><img align="middle" role="math" class="math-img" src="https://bkmyfcolrdumyrwktjrr.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/sat-images/d4413871/img_009_0e89e772.png" alt="the fraction with numerator 2, and denominator, 10 plus x, end fraction, equals one ninth"></span>. Multiplying both sides of this equation by 9 yields <span class="math-container"><img align="middle" role="math" class="math-img" src="https://bkmyfcolrdumyrwktjrr.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/sat-images/d4413871/img_010_2582caae.png" alt="the fraction with numerator 18, and denominator, 10 plus x, end fraction, equals 1"></span>, and multiplying both sides of this equation by <span class="math-container"><img align="middle" role="math" class="math-img" src="https://bkmyfcolrdumyrwktjrr.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/sat-images/d4413871/img_011_589c25f5.png" alt="open parenthesis, 10 plus x, close parenthesis "></span> yields <span class="math-container"><img align="middle" role="math" class="math-img" src="https://bkmyfcolrdumyrwktjrr.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/sat-images/d4413871/img_012_eb73e257.png" alt="18 equals, 10 plus x"></span>. Subtracting 10 from both sides of this equation yields <span class="math-container"><img align="middle" role="math" class="math-img" src="https://bkmyfcolrdumyrwktjrr.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/sat-images/d4413871/img_013_c495e55f.png" alt="8 equals x"></span>.</p>
$SATQ$, true, 14, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, $SATQ$SPR$SATQ$, $SATQ$Math$SATQ$, $SATQ${"questionId":"d4413871","external_id":null,"disclosed_item_id":"019746-DC","source":"disclosed","program":"SAT","test_type":2,"test_type_desc":"Math","primary_class_cd":"Q","domain":"Problem-Solving and Data Analysis","skill_cd":"Q.E.","skill_desc":"Probability and conditional probability","difficulty":"H","score_band_range_cd":6,"type":"spr","stimulus":"<div class=\"stimulus_reference \" xmlns=\"http://www.imsglobal.org/xsd/apip/apipv1p0/qtiitem/imsqti_v2p1\"><div class=\"passage \"><div class=\"prose style:1 \"><p class=\"passage_para \">&nbsp;</p><div class=\"table_wrapper \"><div class=\"tcp-e4589060-6a49-4fb9-a72a-23a578e0b2a9\"><table class=\"table_WithBorder tcp-06196331-3edc-4c8f-876b-d57b3d755f43\"><tbody><tr><td class=\"tcp-06743663-cf51-4d3a-bb0f-8b9210f1b926\">&nbsp;</td><td class=\"tcp-9fb58c64-27a2-4be8-8131-1424067761ce\" colspan=\"4\" rowspan=\"1\">Blood type&nbsp; &nbsp;</td></tr><tr><td class=\"tcp-02abeec4-f408-454a-87df-05c7c6994beb\">Rhesus factor</td><td class=\"tcp-f8b24cc8-81fe-48a7-a682-337ede35519b\">A</td><td class=\"tcp-4bf04f05-b26e-49c9-9e89-3fccdbe67aa5\">B</td><td class=\"tcp-028d81ca-d098-4c84-9e84-3620dbeae02c\">AB</td><td class=\"tcp-02b79468-351b-40a0-b9a7-9b2bb86fe635\">O</td></tr><tr><td class=\"tcp-1aac0023-14d4-4475-935e-069fdbf84bcd\"><span class=\"math_expression \"><span class=\"math-container\"><img align=\"middle\" role=\"math\" class=\"math-img\" src=\"https://bkmyfcolrdumyrwktjrr.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/sat-images/d4413871/img_000_63c9f63f.png\" alt=\"plus\"></span></span></td><td class=\"tcp-05f1a050-4c0d-4e64-b64e-c58780bafe88\">33</td><td class=\"tcp-1d324382-0266-4e24-b80c-3fbd65ce08f7\">9</td><td class=\"tcp-a7adcf0c-ce15-4409-a2e0-667ee9a895e3\">3</td><td class=\"tcp-37dd5d78-47ee-41d7-8c67-420e63f5e677\">37</td></tr><tr><td class=\"tcp-5a3393db-bbc3-4009-b4fc-634ae86ebf04\"><span class=\"math_expression \"><span class=\"math-container\"><img align=\"middle\" role=\"math\" class=\"math-img\" src=\"https://bkmyfcolrdumyrwktjrr.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/sat-images/d4413871/img_001_79bab492.png\" alt=\"minus\"></span></span></td><td class=\"tcp-bd3f95aa-f701-461c-a4d3-ab4c2b64b2ac\">7</td><td class=\"tcp-3ac2333f-1894-4587-9a4e-16bf77125399\">2</td><td class=\"tcp-54b95007-a3cd-44d2-a670-cbf65d2b6c54\">1</td><td class=\"tcp-c50c8657-2486-4a4d-bcfa-e1718c1aee53\"><span class=\"italic\"><span class=\"italic \">x</span></span></td></tr></tbody></table></div></div></div></div></div>\n","stem":"<p class=\"stem_paragraph \">Human blood can be classified into four common blood types&mdash;A, B, AB, and O. It is also characterized by the presence <span class=\"math-container\"><img align=\"middle\" role=\"math\" class=\"math-img\" src=\"https://bkmyfcolrdumyrwktjrr.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/sat-images/d4413871/img_002_e040f3b4.png\" alt=\"open parenthesis, plus, close parenthesis\"></span> or absence <span class=\"math-container\"><img align=\"middle\" role=\"math\" class=\"math-img\" src=\"https://bkmyfcolrdumyrwktjrr.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/sat-images/d4413871/img_003_46d9fd76.png\" alt=\"open parenthesis, minus, close parenthesis\"></span> of the rhesus factor. The table above shows the distribution of blood type and rhesus factor for a group of people. If one of these people who is rhesus negative <span class=\"math-container\"><img align=\"middle\" role=\"math\" class=\"math-img\" src=\"https://bkmyfcolrdumyrwktjrr.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/sat-images/d4413871/img_004_46d9fd76.png\" alt=\"open parenthesis, minus, close parenthesis\"></span> is chosen at random, the probability that the person has blood type B is <span class=\"math_expression \"><span class=\"math-container\"><img align=\"middle\" role=\"math\" class=\"math-img\" src=\"https://bkmyfcolrdumyrwktjrr.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/sat-images/d4413871/img_005_e367f6c9.png\" alt=\"one ninth\"></span></span> . What is the value of <span class=\"italic\">x</span> ?</p>\n","answerOptions":null,"keys":null,"correct_answer":["8"],"rationale":"<p>The correct answer is 8. In this group, <span class=\"math-container\"><img align=\"middle\" role=\"math\" class=\"math-img\" src=\"https://bkmyfcolrdumyrwktjrr.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/sat-images/d4413871/img_006_e367f6c9.png\" alt=\"one ninth\"></span> of the people who are rhesus negative have blood type B. The total number of people who are rhesus negative in the group is <span class=\"math-container\"><img align=\"middle\" role=\"math\" class=\"math-img\" src=\"https://bkmyfcolrdumyrwktjrr.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/sat-images/d4413871/img_007_26860f98.png\" alt=\"7 plus 2, plus 1, plus x\"></span>, and there are 2 people who are rhesus negative with blood type B. Therefore, <span class=\"math-container\"><img align=\"middle\" role=\"math\" class=\"math-img\" src=\"https://bkmyfcolrdumyrwktjrr.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/sat-images/d4413871/img_008_0d0e084f.png\" alt=\"the fraction with numerator 2, and denominator, 7 plus 2, plus 1, plus x, end fraction, equals one ninth\"></span>. Combining like terms on the left-hand side of the equation yields <span class=\"math-container\"><img align=\"middle\" role=\"math\" class=\"math-img\" src=\"https://bkmyfcolrdumyrwktjrr.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/sat-images/d4413871/img_009_0e89e772.png\" alt=\"the fraction with numerator 2, and denominator, 10 plus x, end fraction, equals one ninth\"></span>. Multiplying both sides of this equation by 9 yields <span class=\"math-container\"><img align=\"middle\" role=\"math\" class=\"math-img\" src=\"https://bkmyfcolrdumyrwktjrr.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/sat-images/d4413871/img_010_2582caae.png\" alt=\"the fraction with numerator 18, and denominator, 10 plus x, end fraction, equals 1\"></span>, and multiplying both sides of this equation by <span class=\"math-container\"><img align=\"middle\" role=\"math\" class=\"math-img\" src=\"https://bkmyfcolrdumyrwktjrr.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/sat-images/d4413871/img_011_589c25f5.png\" alt=\"open parenthesis, 10 plus x, close parenthesis \"></span> yields <span class=\"math-container\"><img align=\"middle\" role=\"math\" class=\"math-img\" src=\"https://bkmyfcolrdumyrwktjrr.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/sat-images/d4413871/img_012_eb73e257.png\" alt=\"18 equals, 10 plus x\"></span>. Subtracting 10 from both sides of this equation yields <span class=\"math-container\"><img align=\"middle\" role=\"math\" class=\"math-img\" src=\"https://bkmyfcolrdumyrwktjrr.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/sat-images/d4413871/img_013_c495e55f.png\" alt=\"8 equals x\"></span>.</p>\n","answer_style":"SPR","section":"Math","image_count":14,"raw_list":{"updateDate":1691007959616,"pPcc":"SAT#Q","questionId":"d4413871","skill_cd":"Q.E.","score_band_range_cd":6,"skill_desc":"Probability and conditional probability","createDate":1691007959616,"program":"SAT","primary_class_cd_desc":"Problem-Solving and Data Analysis","ibn":"019746-DC","external_id":null,"primary_class_cd":"Q","uId":"1eb20a8c-7806-4bd7-8d92-aa013d25e954","difficulty":"H"},"raw_detail":{"item_id":"019746-DC","section":"Math","body":"<div class=\"stimulus_reference \" xmlns=\"http://www.imsglobal.org/xsd/apip/apipv1p0/qtiitem/imsqti_v2p1\"><div class=\"passage \"><div class=\"prose style:1 \"><p class=\"passage_para \">&nbsp;</p><div class=\"table_wrapper \"><div class=\"tcp-e4589060-6a49-4fb9-a72a-23a578e0b2a9\"><table class=\"table_WithBorder tcp-06196331-3edc-4c8f-876b-d57b3d755f43\"><tbody><tr><td class=\"tcp-06743663-cf51-4d3a-bb0f-8b9210f1b926\">&nbsp;</td><td class=\"tcp-9fb58c64-27a2-4be8-8131-1424067761ce\" colspan=\"4\" rowspan=\"1\">Blood type&nbsp; &nbsp;</td></tr><tr><td class=\"tcp-02abeec4-f408-454a-87df-05c7c6994beb\">Rhesus factor</td><td class=\"tcp-f8b24cc8-81fe-48a7-a682-337ede35519b\">A</td