,3.78,0,0,1,245.319,37.478Z\"></path><path d=\"M352.688,79.056a3.78,3.78,0,1,1-3.778-3.78A3.777,3.777,0,0,1,352.688,79.056Z\"></path><path d=\"M352.688,65.2a3.78,3.78,0,1,1-3.778-3.78A3.779,3.779,0,0,1,352.688,65.2Z\"></path><path d=\"M352.688,51.339a3.78,3.78,0,1,1-3.778-3.78A3.776,3.776,0,0,1,352.688,51.339Z\"></path><path d=\"M352.688,37.478a3.78,3.78,0,1,1-3.778-3.78A3.78,3.78,0,0,1,352.688,37.478Z\"></path><path d=\"M218.479,79.056a3.78,3.78,0,1,1-3.778-3.78A3.778,3.778,0,0,1,218.479,79.056Z\"></path><path d=\"M218.479,65.2a3.78,3.78,0,1,1-3.778-3.78A3.78,3.78,0,0,1,218.479,65.2Z\"></path><path d=\"M379.059,79.056a3.78,3.78,0,1,1-3.778-3.78A3.777,3.777,0,0,1,379.059,79.056Z\"></path><path d=\"M379.059,65.2a3.78,3.78,0,1,1-3.778-3.78A3.779,3.779,0,0,1,379.059,65.2Z\"></path></g></svg><div role=\"region\" aria-label=\"Long description for 2 dot plots titled Data Set A and Data Set B\" class=\"sr-only\"><ul>\n<li>For the dot plot titled Data Set A:\n<ul>\n<li>The number line ranges from 10 to 16 in increments of 1.</li>\n<li>The data for the dot plot are as follows:\n<ul>\n<li>10: 1 dot</li>\n<li>11: 4 dots</li>\n<li>12: 2 dots</li>\n<li>13: 3 dots</li>\n<li>14: 2 dots</li>\n<li>15: 4 dots</li>\n<li>16: 1 dot</li>\n</ul>\n</li>\n</ul>\n</li>\n<li>For the dot plot titled Data Set B:\n<ul>\n<li>The number line ranges from 10 to 16 in increments of 1.</li>\n<li>The data for the dot plot are as follows:\n<ul>\n<li>10: 2 dots</li>\n<li>11: 4 dots</li>\n<li>12: 2 dots</li>\n<li>13: 1 dot</li>\n<li>14: 2 dots</li>\n<li>15: 4 dots</li>\n<li>16: 2 dots</li>\n</ul>\n</li>\n</ul>\n</li>\n</ul></div></figure></p>\n<p style=\"text-align: left;\">Which of the following statements must be true?</p>\n<ol style=\"list-style-type: upper-roman;\">\n<li style=\"text-align: left;\">The median of data set A is equal to the median of data set B.</li>\n<li style=\"text-align: left;\">The standard deviation of data set A is equal to the standard deviation of data set B.</li>\n</ol>","externalid":"bb8df1b9-8ab9-42bb-8b7f-adec3639c7f8","templateid":"11df673e-7fcf-4b4e-a696-c6d91bf7ee70","vaultid":"746f9397-d7f7-40b3-95f6-2aed24a0de39","type":"mcq","answerOptions":[{"id":"b0b7e54e-6d7a-4dff-a0cf-2c5bb1f9a4ba","content":"<p style=\"text-align: left;\">I only</p>"},{"id":"3d576ac6-dbc0-402f-88b3-347799774f48","content":"<p style=\"text-align: left;\">II only</p>"},{"id":"9e7909ec-9a55-4b6f-a08c-2e461d1960e2","content":"<p style=\"text-align: left;\">I and II</p>"},{"id":"e1b52faa-a064-4a6c-bb9e-400409f1cb84","content":"<p style=\"text-align: left;\">Neither I nor II</p>"}],"correct_answer":["A"]},"createDate":1691007959833,"updateDate":1691007959833}$SATQ$::jsonb, 1691007959833, 1691007959833),
    ($SATQ$d693f563$SATQ$, $SATQ$47d32f6a-d945-4d6e-9f0f-18a983b72be4$SATQ$::uuid, $SATQ$ba9043d2-69bd-437a-9c81-febd61cc891a$SATQ$::uuid, NULL, $SATQ$qbank$SATQ$, $SATQ$SAT$SATQ$, 2, $SATQ$Math$SATQ$, $SATQ$Problem-Solving and Data Analysis$SATQ$, $SATQ$Q$SATQ$, $SATQ$Q.B.$SATQ$, $SATQ$Percentages$SATQ$, $SATQ$M$SATQ$, 4, $SATQ$spr$SATQ$, NULL, $SATQ$<p>Last year, Cedric had <math alttext="35"><mn>35</mn>
</math> plants in his garden. This year, the number of plants in Cedric&rsquo;s garden is <math alttext="60 percent sign"><mn>60</mn>
<mo>%</mo></math> greater than the number of plants in his garden last year. How many plants does Cedric have in his garden this year?</p>$SATQ$, $SATQ$[]$SATQ$::jsonb, $SATQ$["56"]$SATQ$::jsonb, $SATQ$["56"]$SATQ$::jsonb, $SATQ$<p style="text-align: left;">The correct answer is <math alttext="56"><mn>56</mn>
</math>. It&rsquo;s given that Cedric had <math alttext="35"><mn>35</mn>
</math> plants in his garden last year and that the number of plants in Cedric's garden this year is <math alttext="60 percent sign"><mn>60</mn><mo>%</mo></math> greater than the number of plants in his garden last year. It follows that the number of plants in Cedric&rsquo;s garden this year is <math alttext="35"><mn>35</mn>
</math> plus <math alttext="60 percent sign"><mn>60</mn><mo>%</mo></math> of <math alttext="35"><mn>35</mn>
</math>, which is equal to <math alttext="35 plus 35 left parenthesis StartFraction 60 Over 100 EndFraction right parenthesis"><mn>35</mn><mo>+</mo><mn>35</mn><mfenced><mfrac><mn>60</mn><mn>100</mn></mfrac></mfenced></math>, or <math alttext="35 plus 35 left parenthesis 0.6 right parenthesis"><mn>35</mn><mo>+</mo><mn>35</mn><mfenced><mn>0.6</mn></mfenced></math>. This expression is equivalent to <math alttext="35 plus 21"><mn>35</mn><mo>+</mo><mn>21</mn></math>, or <math alttext="56"><mn>56</mn>
</math>. Therefore, Cedric has <math alttext="56"><mn>56</mn>
</math> plants in his garden this year.</p>$SATQ$, false, 0, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, $SATQ$manifold$SATQ$, NULL, NULL, NULL, $SATQ${"questionId":"d693f563","external_id":"47d32f6a-d945-4d6e-9f0f-18a983b72be4","disclosed_item_id":null,"source":"qbank","vaultid":"ba9043d2-69bd-437a-9c81-febd61cc891a","uId":"3cc34195-16f7-4655-82eb-30834118dfb7","program":"SAT","test_type":2,"test_type_desc":"Math","primary_class_cd":"Q","domain":"Problem-Solving and Data Analysis","skill_cd":"Q.B.","skill_desc":"Percentages","difficulty":"M","score_band_range_cd":4,"type":"spr","stimulus":null,"stem":"<p>Last year, Cedric had <math alttext=\"35\"><mn>35</mn>\n</math> plants in his garden. This year, the number of plants in Cedric&rsquo;s garden is <math alttext=\"60 percent sign\"><mn>60</mn>\n<mo>%</mo></math> greater than the number of plants in his garden last year. How many plants does Cedric have in his garden this year?</p>","answerOptions":[],"keys":["56"],"correct_answer":["56"],"rationale":"<p style=\"text-align: left;\">The correct answer is <math alttext=\"56\"><mn>56</mn>\n</math>. It&rsquo;s given that Cedric had <math alttext=\"35\"><mn>35</mn>\n</math> plants in his garden last year and that the number of plants in Cedric's garden this year is <math alttext=\"60 percent sign\"><mn>60</mn><mo>%</mo></math> greater than the number of plants in his garden last year. It follows that the number of plants in Cedric&rsquo;s garden this year is <math alttext=\"35\"><mn>35</mn>\n</math> plus <math alttext=\"60 percent sign\"><mn>60</mn><mo>%</mo></math> of <math alttext=\"35\"><mn>35</mn>\n</math>, which is equal to <math alttext=\"35 plus 35 left parenthesis StartFraction 60 Over 100 EndFraction right parenthesis\"><mn>35</mn><mo>+</mo><mn>35</mn><mfenced><mfrac><mn>60</mn><mn>100</mn></mfrac></mfenced></math>, or <math alttext=\"35 plus 35 left parenthesis 0.6 right parenthesis\"><mn>35</mn><mo>+</mo><mn>35</mn><mfenced><mn>0.6</mn></mfenced></math>. This expression is equival