</math> can be calculated by solving the equation&nbsp;<math alttext="17.36 equals left parenthesis StartFraction p Over 100 EndFraction right parenthesis left parenthesis 15.50 right parenthesis"><mn>17.36</mn><mo>=</mo><mfenced><mfrac><mi>p</mi><mn>100</mn></mfrac></mfenced><mfenced><mn>15.50</mn></mfenced></math>, or&nbsp;<math alttext="17.36 equals StartFraction 15.50 p Over 100 EndFraction"><mn>17.36</mn><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mrow><mn>15.50</mn><mi>p</mi></mrow><mn>100</mn></mfrac></math>. Multiplying each side of this equation by <math alttext="100"><mn>100</mn>
</math> yields&nbsp;<math alttext="1,736 equals 15.50 p"><mn>1,736</mn><mo>=</mo><mn>15.50</mn><mi>p</mi></math>. Dividing each side of this equation by&nbsp;<math alttext="15.50"><mn>15.50</mn></math> yields <math alttext="112 equals p"><mrow>
	<mn>112</mn>
	<mo>=</mo>
	<mi>p</mi>
</mrow>
</math>. Therefore, the value of <math alttext="p"><mi>p</mi>
