,0,1,1-3.778-3.78A3.78,3.78,0,0,1,336.8,74.828Z\"></path><path d=\"M336.8,60.971a3.78,3.78,0,1,1-3.778-3.78A3.78,3.78,0,0,1,336.8,60.971Z\"></path><line x1=\"398.299\" y1=\"131.346\" x2=\"214.159\" y2=\"131.346\" fill=\"none\" stroke=\"#000\" stroke-linecap=\"round\" stroke-linejoin=\"round\" stroke-width=\"0.945\"></line><line x1=\"358.964\" y1=\"125.676\" x2=\"358.964\" y2=\"137.016\" fill=\"none\" stroke=\"#000\" stroke-linecap=\"round\" stroke-linejoin=\"round\" stroke-width=\"0.945\"></line><line x1=\"229.224\" y1=\"125.676\" x2=\"229.224\" y2=\"137.016\" fill=\"none\" stroke=\"#000\" stroke-linecap=\"round\" stroke-linejoin=\"round\" stroke-width=\"0.945\"></line><line x1=\"384.911\" y1=\"125.676\" x2=\"384.911\" y2=\"137.016\" fill=\"none\" stroke=\"#000\" stroke-linecap=\"round\" stroke-linejoin=\"round\" stroke-width=\"0.945\"></line><line x1=\"255.171\" y1=\"125.676\" x2=\"255.171\" y2=\"137.016\" fill=\"none\" stroke=\"#000\" stroke-linecap=\"round\" stroke-linejoin=\"round\" stroke-width=\"0.945\"></line><line x1=\"281.121\" y1=\"125.676\" x2=\"281.121\" y2=\"137.016\" fill=\"none\" stroke=\"#000\" stroke-linecap=\"round\" stroke-linejoin=\"round\" stroke-width=\"0.945\"></line><line x1=\"307.07\" y1=\"125.676\" x2=\"307.07\" y2=\"137.016\" fill=\"none\" stroke=\"#000\" stroke-linecap=\"round\" stroke-linejoin=\"round\" stroke-width=\"0.945\"></line><line x1=\"333.017\" y1=\"125.676\" x2=\"333.017\" y2=\"137.016\" fill=\"none\" stroke=\"#000\" stroke-linecap=\"round\" stroke-linejoin=\"round\" stroke-width=\"0.945\"></line></g></svg><div role=\"region\" aria-label=\"Long description for 2 dot plots titled Class A and Class B\" class=\"sr-only\"><ul>\n<li>For the dot plot titled Class A:<br>\n<ul>\n<li>The number line ranges from 1 to 7 in increments of 1.</li>\n<li>The data for the dot plot are as follows:<br>\n<ul>\n<li>1: 1 dot</li>\n<li>2: 1 dot</li>\n<li>3: 3 dots</li>\n<li>4: 4 dots</li>\n<li>5: 5 dots</li>\n<li>6: 6 dots</li>\n<li>7: 7 dots</li>\n</ul>\n</li>\n</ul>\n</li>\n<li>For the dot plot titled Class B:<br>\n<ul>\n<li>The number line ranges from 14 to 20 in increments of 1.</li>\n<li>The data for the dot plot are as follows:<br>\n<ul>\n<li>14: 1 dot</li>\n<li>15: 1 dot</li>\n<li>16: 3 dots</li>\n<li>17: 4 dots</li>\n<li>18: 5 dots</li>\n<li>19: 6 dots</li>\n<li>20: 7 dots</li>\n</ul>\n</li>\n</ul>\n</li>\n</ul></div></figure></p>\n<p style=\"text-align: left;\">Each of the dot plots shown represents the number of glue sticks brought in by each student for two classes, class A and class B. Which statement best compares the standard deviations of the numbers of glue sticks brought in by each student for these two classes?</p>","externalid":"5af384de-ab0c-40e8-8d4d-b12e04a08e8e","templateid":"819a6f43-1a3a-466a-8b28-2e21063aacc2","vaultid":"3e59621e-5a98-4b6f-b9f7-269759e80626","type":"mcq","answerOptions":[{"id":"77214f2d-c0a9-43b7-8770-9996641c119a","content":"<p style=\"text-align: left;\">The standard deviation of the number of glue sticks brought in by each student for class A is less than the standard deviation of the number of glue sticks brought in by each student for class B.</p>"},{"id":"7b924b30-5c15-4579-b52c-6a0b4dae7cf6","content":"<p style=\"text-align: left;\">The standard deviation of the number of glue sticks brought in by each student for class A is equal to the standard deviation of the number of glue sticks brought in by each student for class B.</p>"},{"id":"35045890-3585-4ec6-8a27-14facdf7d14b","content":"<p style=\"text-align: left;\">The standard deviation of the number of glue sticks brought in by each student for class A is greater than the standard deviation of the number of glue sticks brought in by each student for class B.</p>"},{"id":"b4c273fe-545c-463a-8729-dc537d454bb7","content":"<p style=\"text-align: left;\">There is not enough information to compare these standard deviations.</p>"}],"correct_answer":["B"]},"createDate":1691007959833,"updateDate":1691007959833}$SATQ$::jsonb, 1691007959833, 1691007959833),
    ($SATQ$da9ffcf6$SATQ$, $SATQ$688b466f-c743-40b5-8bd7-7b8695af38e7$SATQ$::uuid, NULL, NULL, $SATQ$qbank$SATQ$, $SATQ$SAT$SATQ$, 2, $SATQ$Math$SATQ$, $SATQ$Problem-Solving and Data Analysis$SATQ$, $SATQ$Q$SATQ$, $SATQ$Q.A.$SATQ$, $SATQ$Ratios, rates, proportional relationships, and units$SATQ$, $SATQ$E$SATQ$, 3, $SATQ$mcq$SATQ$, NULL, $SATQ$<p style="text-align: left;">The ratio of the length of line segment <math alttext="upper X upper Y"><mi>X</mi><mi>Y</mi></math> to the length of line segment <math alttext="upper Z upper V"><mi>Z</mi><mi>V</mi></math> is <math alttext="6"><mn>6</mn>
</math> to <math alttext="1"><mn>1</mn>
</math>. If the length of line segment <math alttext="upper X upper Y"><mi>X</mi><mi>Y</mi></math> is <math alttext="102"><mn>102</mn>
</math> inches, what is the length, in inches, of line segment <math alttext="upper Z upper V"><mi>Z</mi><mi>V</mi></math>?</p>$SATQ$, $SATQ$[{"id":"deb55e4d-de7c-40f0-8ada-a88570f76597","content":"<p><math alttext=\"17\"><mn>17</mn>\n</math></p>"},{"id":"086949a2-0b0e-44a6-ad15-63fa2d9d92ec","content":"<p><math alttext=\"96\"><mn>96</mn>\n</math></p>"},{"id":"3dc9eefa-09d4-438b-aa69-e13948f4229f","content":"<p><math alttext=\"102\"><mn>102</mn>\n</math></p>"},{"id":"e4288ad6-fb2b-402c-93e6-dce1823cf478","content":"<p><math alttext=\"612\"><mn>612</mn>\n</math></p>"}]$SATQ$::jsonb, $SATQ$["A"]$SATQ$::jsonb, $SATQ$["deb55e4d-de7c-40f0-8ada-a88570f76597"]$SATQ$::jsonb, $SATQ$<p style="text-align: left;">Choice A is correct. It&rsquo;s given that the ratio of the length of line segment <math alttext="upper X upper Y"><mi>X</mi><mi>Y</mi></math> to the length of line segment <math alttext="upper Z upper V"><mi>Z</mi><mi>V</mi></math> is <math alttext="6"><mn>6</mn>
</math> to <math alttext="1"><mn>1</mn>
</math>, which means <math alttext="StartFraction upper X upper Y Over upper Z upper V EndFraction equals six oneths"><mfrac><mrow><mi>X</mi><mi>Y</mi></mrow><mrow><mi>Z</mi><mi>V</mi></mrow></mfrac><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mn>6</mn><mn>1</mn></mfrac></math>. It&rsquo;s given that the length of line segment <math alttext="upper X upper Y"><mi>X</mi><mi>Y</mi></math> is <math alttext="102"><mn>102</mn>
</math> inches. If the length, in inches, of line segment <math alttext="upper Z upper V"><mi>Z</mi><mi>V</mi></math> is represented by <math alttext="script l"><mi mathvariant="script">l</mi></math>, the value of <math alttext="script l"><mi mathvariant="script">l</mi></math> can be calculated by solving the equation <math alttext="StartFraction 102 Over script l EndFraction equals six oneths"><mfrac><mn>102</mn><mi mathvariant="script">l</mi></mfrac><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mn>6</mn><mn>1</mn></mfrac></math>, or <math alttext="StartFraction 102 Over script l EndFraction equals 6"><mfrac><mn>102</mn><mi mathvariant="script">l</mi></mfrac><mo>=</mo><mn>6</mn></math>. Multiplying each side of this equation by <math alttext="script l"><mi mathvariant="script">l</mi></math> yields <math alttext="102 equals 6 script l"><mn>102</mn><mo>=</mo><mn>6</mn><mi mathvariant="script">l</mi></math>. Dividing each side of this equation by <math alttext="6"><mn>6</mn>
</math> yields <math alttext="17 equals script l"><mn>17</mn><mo>=</mo><mi mathvariant="script">l</mi></math>. Therefore, the length of line segment <math alttext="upper Z upper V"><mi>Z</mi><mi>V</mi></math> is <math alttext="17"><mn>17</mn>
</math> inches.</p>
<p style="text-align: left;">Choice B is incorrect. This is the length, in inches, of line segment <math alttext="upper Z upper V"><mi>Z</mi><mi>V</mi></math> if the length of line segment <math alttext="upper X upper Y"><mi>X</mi><mi>Y</mi></math> is <math alttext="576"><mn>576</mn>
</math>, not <math alttext="102"><mn>102</mn>
</math>, inches.</p>
<p style="text-align: left;">Choice C is incorrect. This is the length, in inches, of line segment <math alttext="upper X upper Y"><mi>X</mi><mi>Y</mi></math>, not line segment <math alttext="upper Z upper V"><mi>Z</mi><mi>V</mi></math>.</p>
<p style="text-align: left;">Choice D is incorrect. This is the length, in inches, of line segment <math alttext="upper Z upper V"><mi>Z</mi><mi>V</mi></math> if the ratio of the length of line segment <math alttext="upper X upper Y"><mi>X</mi><mi>Y</mi></math> to the length of line segment <math alttext="upper Z upper V"><mi>Z</mi><mi>V</mi></math> is <math alttext="1"><mn>1</mn>
</math> to <math alttext="6"><mn>6</mn>
</math>, not <math alttext="6"><mn>6</mn>
</math> to <math alttext="1"><mn>1</mn>
</math>.</p>$SATQ$, false, 0, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, $SATQ${"questionId":"da9ffcf6","external_id":"688b466f-c743-40b5-8bd7-7b8695af38e7","disclosed_item_id":null,"source":"qbank","vaultid":null,"uId":"29862eb4-8ed7-4ad8-897a-7d9e287e54e0","program":"SAT","test_type":2,"test_type_desc":"Math","primary_class_cd":"Q","domain":"Problem-Solving and Data Analysis","skill_cd":"Q.A.","skill_desc":"Ratios, rates, proportional relationships, and units","difficulty":"E","score_band_range_cd":3,"type":"mcq","stimulus":null,"stem":"<p style=\"text-align: left;\">The ratio of the length of line segment <math alttext=\"upper X upper Y\"><mi>X</mi><mi>Y</mi></math> to the length of line segment <math alttext=\"upper Z upper V\"><mi>Z</mi><mi>V</mi></math> is <math alttext=\"6\"><mn>6</mn>\n</math> to <math alttext=\"1\"><mn>1</mn>\n</math>. If the length of line segment <math alttext=\"upper X upper Y\"><mi>X</mi><mi>Y</mi></math> is <math alttext=\"102\"><mn>102</mn>\n</math> inches, what is the length, in inches, of line segment <math alttext=\"upper Z upper V\"><mi>Z</mi><mi>V</mi></math>?</p>","answerOptions":[{"id":"deb55e4d-de7c-40f0-8ada-a88570f76597","content":"<p><math alttext=\"17\"><mn>17</mn>\n</math></p>"},{"id":"086949a2-0b0e-44a6-ad15-63fa2d9d92ec","content":"<p><math alttext=\"96\"><mn>96</mn>\n</math></p>"},{"id":"3dc9eefa-09d4-438b-aa69-e13948f4229f","content":"<p><math alttext=\"102\"><mn>102</mn>\n</math></p>"},{"id":"e4288ad6-fb2b-402c-93e6-dce1823cf478","content":"<p><math alttext=\"612\"><mn>612</mn>\n</math></p>"}],"keys":["deb55e4d-de7c-40f0-8ada-a88570f76597"],"correct_answer":["A"],"rationale":"<p style=\"text-align: left;\">Choice A is correct. It&rsquo;s given that the ratio of the length of line segment <math alttext=\"upper X upper Y\"><mi>X</mi><mi>Y</mi></math> to the length of line segment <math alttext=\"upper Z upper V\"><mi>Z</mi><mi>V</mi></math> is <math alttext=\"6\"><mn>6</mn>\n</math> to <math alttext=\"1\"><mn>1</m