<div role="region" aria-label="Long description for scatterplot" class="sr-only"><ul>
<li>The scatterplot has 10 data points.</li>
<li>The data points are in a linear pattern trending up from left to right.</li>
<li>A line of best fit is shown:<br>
<ul>
<li>The line of best fit slants up from left to right.</li>
<li>6 points are above the line of best fit.</li>
<li>4 points are below the line of best fit.</li>
<li>The line of best fit passes through the following approximate coordinates:<br>
<ul>
<li>(0 comma 0.1)</li>
<li>(5 comma 5.1)</li>
</ul>
</li>
</ul>
</li>
</ul></div></figure></p>
<p style="text-align: left;">For how many of the <math alttext="10"><mn>10</mn>
</math> data points is the actual <em>y</em>-value greater than the <em>y</em>-value predicted by the line of best fit?</p>$SATQ$, $SATQ$[{"id":"560b7581-5a76-49eb-9190-a2483f8e5b25","content":"<p><math alttext=\"3\"><mn>3</mn>\n</math></p>"},{"id":"d23d7872-970a-4a59-bac2-c51f3ab8f642","content":"<p><math alttext=\"4\"><mn>4</mn>\n</math></p>"},{"id":"8262b99c-a5e1-440f-ae8d-bb713c6031e1","content":"<p><math alttext=\"6\"><mn>6</mn>\n</math></p>"},{"id":"adad886e-ac51-4df6-8636-a3dbf55f375a","content":"<p><math alttext=\"7\"><mn>7</mn>\n</math></p>"}]$SATQ$::jsonb, $SATQ$["C"]$SATQ$::jsonb, $SATQ$["8262b99c-a5e1-440f-ae8d-bb713c6031e1"]$SATQ$::jsonb, $SATQ$<p style="text-align: left;">Choice C is correct. Any data point that's located above the line of best fit has a <em>y</em>-value that's greater than the <em>y</em>-value predicted by the line of best fit. For the scatterplot shown, <math alttext="6"><mn>6</mn>
</math> of the data points are above the line of best fit. Therefore, <math alttext="6"><mn>6</mn>
</math> of the data points have an actual <em>y</em>-value that's greater than the <em>y</em>-value predicted by the line of best fit.</p>
<p style="text-align: left;">Choice A is incorrect and may result from conceptual or calculation errors.</p>
<p style="text-align: left;">Choice B is incorrect. This is the number of data points that have an actual <em>y</em>-value that's less than the <em>y</em>-value predicted by the line of best fit.</p>
<p style="text-align: left;">Choice D is incorrect and may result from conceptual or calculation errors.</p>$SATQ$, false, 0, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, $SATQ${"questionId":"e17babed","external_id":"03f22abf-7da2-44d7-9e60-a131e0841a87","disclosed_item_id":null,"source":"qbank","vaultid":null,"uId":"4f1adae8-476d-4ff9-b19a-1d1ee1eb7a47","program":"SAT","test_type":2,"test_type_desc":"Math","primary_class_cd":"Q","domain":"Problem-Solving and Data Analysis","skill_cd":"Q.D.","skill_desc":"Two-variable data: Models and scatterplots","difficulty":"M","score_band_range_cd":4,"type":"mcq","stimulus":null,"stem":"<p style=\"text-align: left;\">The scatterplot shows the relationship between two variables, <math alttext=\"x\"><mi>x</mi>\n</math> and <math alttext=\"y\"><mi>y</mi>\n</math>. A line of best fit for the data is also shown.</p>\n<p style=\"text-align: center;\"><figure class='image'><svg height=\"275.22pt\" version=\"1.1\" viewBox=\"0 0 286.56 275.22\" width=\"286.56pt\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg\" xmlns:xlink=\"http://www.w3.org/1999/xlink\" role=\"img\" aria-label=\"A scatterplot in the x y plane with the origin labeled O. The x axis ranges from 0 to 10. The y axis ranges from 0 to 10. Refer to long description.\">\n <defs>\n  <style type=\"text/css\">\n*{stroke-linecap:butt;stroke-linejoin:round;}\n  </style>\n </defs>\n <g id=\"figure_1\">\n  <g id=\"patch_1\">\n   <path d=\"M 0 275.22 \nL 286.56 275.22 \nL 286.56 0 \nL 0 0 \nz\n\" style=\"fill:none;\"></path>\n  </g>\n  <g id=\"axes_1\">\n   <g id=\"patch_2\">\n    <path d=\"M 7.2 260.46 \nL 279.36 260.46 \nL 279.36 10.98 \nL 7.2 10.98 \nz\n\" style=\"fill:none;\"></path>\n   </g>\n   <g id=\"matplotlib.axis_1\"></g>\n   <g id=\"matplotlib.axis_2\"></g>\n  </g>\n  <g id=\"axes_2\">\n   <g id=\"patch_3\">\n    <path d=\"M 9.200821 268.02 \nL 271.689179 268.02 \nL 271.689179 7.2 \nL 9.200821 7.2 \nz\n\" style=\"fill:none;\"></path>\n   </g>\n   <g id=\"matplotlib.axis_3\">\n    <